From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:38:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs42l84: acknowledge the remote status latch
 under macOS's probe sequence

The J604's headset codec still raised about 1000 interrupts a second
with nothing plugged in after the plug-interrupt masks were set as
macOS sets them: the masks were not the source.

macOS's probe writes (apple,init-writes) set 0x1480 from 0xe0 to 0x80,
unmasking bits 5 and 6. Their status latches in REMOTE_BUTTON_STATUS1
(0x1484) at power-up: macOS reads it as 0x60 13 ms after the write, the
read clears it (it reads 0x00 after), and macOS sees no codec traffic
at idle. This driver never read 0x1484 outside button polling, so the
latch held the interrupt line asserted, and every interrupt cost two
I2C reads that changed nothing.

With the init writes, read 0x1484 once after them and on every codec
interrupt, as macOS does. The polled button bits (0 and 1) are not
affected: the poll reads the same register at its own cadence.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c
index 96f822d152..3982bfa1ca 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l84.c
@@ -1011,6 +1011,13 @@ static irqreturn_t cs42l84_irq_thread(int irq, void *data)
 	}
 
 	if (cs42l84->ring_detect) {
+		/*
+		 * macOS's probe writes unmask two more sources in 0x1480 (bits
+		 * 5 and 6); their status latches in REMOTE_BUTTON_STATUS1 and is
+		 * cleared by reading it, which macOS's handler does. Unread, it
+		 * holds the interrupt line asserted for good.
+		 */
+		regmap_read(cs42l84->regmap, CS42L84_REMOTE_BUTTON_STATUS1, &reg);
 		regmap_read(cs42l84->regmap, CS42L84_TSRS_PLUG_STATUS, &reg);
 		current_ring_state = (((char)reg) &
 		      (CS42L84_RS_PLUG | CS42L84_RS_UNPLUG)) >>
@@ -1304,6 +1311,9 @@ static int cs42l84_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c_client)
 	ret = cs42l84_apply_init_writes(cs42l84);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_shutdown;
+	/* The sources they unmask come up latched (0x60): clear them now. */
+	if (cs42l84->ring_detect)
+		regmap_read(cs42l84->regmap, CS42L84_REMOTE_BUTTON_STATUS1, &reg);
 
 	/* Setup plug detection */
 	cs42l84_setup_plug_detect(cs42l84);
-- 
2.43.0

